  "id": "infantile-autism",
  "term": "infantile autism",
  "definition": "Infantile autism is described here as a severe form of autism spectrum disorder marked by difficulties in social behavior. In this account, it involves impairments in both joint and group-based shared intentionality, linked to problems with mind reading, being influenced by others’ intentions, and taking another perspective.",
